# Spiffy Components - Visual Consistency Rules

This React component library uses vanilla CSS with CSS Modules for styling. Follow these rules to maintain visual consistency across all components.

## CSS Module Structure

- All component styles MUST use CSS Modules (`.module.css` files)
- Each component should have its own `ComponentName.module.css` file
- Import CSS modules directly: `import './ComponentName.module.css';`
- NEVER use inline styles or global CSS classes for component-specific styling
- CSS modules are scoped automatically - use them for all component styling
- All styling and behavior should be HTML/CSS first.  
  - Vision is to have as much styling and behavior that could be reused outside React as possible (Vue, Angular, Vanilla HTML) by importing the CSS file and assigning classes to HTML elements.

## Class Naming Conventions

- All component classes MUST use the `sc-` prefix (e.g., `.sc-button`, `.sc-accordion`)
- Use kebab-case for class names: `.sc-component-name`
- Nested elements use compound names: `.sc-component-element` (e.g., `.sc-button-content`, `.sc-accordion-heading`)
- BEM-like structure but with `sc-` prefix: `.sc-component`, `.sc-component-element`, `.sc-component-element-modifier`
- Examples:
  - Component: `.sc-button`
  - Element: `.sc-button-content`, `.sc-accordion-heading`
  - Modifier: `.sc-button-busy` (when needed as a separate class)

## CSS Variable Patterns

- Define component-specific CSS variables in `:root` within each module file
- Group variables by category with clear comments:
  - `/* Component Sizing & Spacing - Using design system tokens as defaults */`
  - `/* Component Typography */`
  - `/* Component Theming - Default colors */`
- Use design system tokens as defaults (e.g., `var(--spacing-padding-2)`, `var(--font-size-2)`)
- Component variables should follow pattern: `--component-name-property` (e.g., `--button-padding`, `--accordion-border-color`)
- Always reference design tokens rather than hardcoding values

## Color System (spiffy-colors)

- ALWAYS use CSS variables from spiffy-colors, NEVER hardcoded colors
- The spiffy-colors package provides base color scales that are mapped to semantic colors
- Use semantic color mappings from the default theme:
  - Base/Neutral: `--base-1` through `--base-12` (1 = lightest, 12 = darkest)
  - Primary: `--primary-1` through `--primary-12`
  - Success: `--success-1` through `--success-12`
  - Warning: `--warning-1` through `--warning-12`
  - Alert/Error: `--alert-1` through `--alert-12`
- For variants, typically use:
  - Backgrounds: scale 10-12 (theme colors will automatically switch between light and dark modes as long as it's configured correctly)
  - Borders/Accents: scale 6-9 (medium emphasis)
  - Text: scale 1-3 (theme colors will automatically switch between light and dark modes as long as it's configured correctly)
- Theme colors automatically switch between light and dark modes when configured correctly in the default theme
- Reference: `lib/components/Theme/themes/default-theme.css` for semantic mappings
- Import spiffy-colors CSS in AppRoot: `import '@spiffdog/spiffy-colors/dist/index.css';`

## Design Token Usage

- **Spacing**: Use `--spacing-padding-*` and `--spacing-gap-*` (0-8 scale)
  - Example: `padding: var(--spacing-padding-2);`
- **Typography**: Use `--font-size-*` (0-8), `--font-weight-*`, `--font-line-height`
  - Example: `font-size: var(--font-size-2);`
- **Border Radius**: Use `--border-radius-*` (0-5, plus `--border-radius-rounded`)
  - Example: `border-radius: var(--border-radius-0);`
- **Animation**: Use `--animation-speed` for transitions
  - Example: `transition: all var(--animation-speed) ease-in-out;`
- NEVER hardcode spacing, font sizes, or border radius values
- Always reference design tokens to maintain consistency

## Variant Patterns & Data Attributes

- **CRITICAL: Use data attributes for ALL simple state values** - NEVER use className toggles for variants, appearance, or boolean states
- Use `data-variant` attribute for color variants: `data-variant="primary"`, `data-variant="alert"`, `data-variant="success"`, `data-variant="warning"`, `data-variant="base"`
- Use `data-appearance` attribute for style variants: `data-appearance="basic"`, `data-appearance="outline"`, `data-appearance="solid"`, `data-appearance="text"`, `data-appearance="contained"`, `data-appearance="elevated"`
- Use `data-rounded` for border radius toggles: `data-rounded="true"` or `data-rounded="false"`
- Use `data-size` for size variants: `data-size="xs"`, `data-size="sm"`, `data-size="md"`, `data-size="lg"`, `data-size="xl"`, `data-size="x2"`
- Use `data-closable` for closable components: `data-closable="true"`
- Use `data-compact` for compact variants: `data-compact="true"`
- Target data attributes in CSS: `.sc-component[data-variant='primary']`, `.sc-component[data-rounded='true']`
- Override component CSS variables within variant selectors
- In JSX, set data attributes directly: `<div className="sc-component" data-variant={variant} data-rounded={rounded} />`
- Boolean data attributes: Use string values `"true"` or `"false"` (e.g., `data-rounded="true"`)
- Example CSS:
  ```css
  .sc-component[data-variant='primary'] {
      --component-theme-color: var(--primary-10);
  }
  .sc-component[data-rounded='true'] {
      border-radius: var(--border-radius-rounded);
  }
  ```

## State Management (Hover, Disabled, Focus)

- **Use data attributes for component state values** - Track simple state like variants, appearance, rounded, closable, compact, size, etc. via data attributes
- Use `color-mix()` for hover and disabled states:
  - Hover: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-color) 90%, white)`
  - Disabled: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-color) 50%, transparent)`
- For disabled states, use opacity mixing: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-color) 50%, transparent)`
- ALWAYS include `:hover`, `:disabled`, `:focus`, and `:focus-visible` states
- Use `transition: all var(--animation-speed) ease-in-out` for smooth state changes
- Support dark appearance with `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` when a hover/focus rule needs a different mix than in light mode (do not rely on `data-theme` for color scheme)
- For complex interactive states (open/closed, active), use native HTML attributes when possible:
  - `[open]` for details element
  - `:checked` for inputs
  - `:disabled` for form elements
- Example:
  ```css
  .sc-component:hover {
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-color) 90%, white);
  }
  .sc-component:disabled {
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--theme-color) 50%, transparent);
      cursor: not-allowed;
  }
  ```

## Component Structure

- Define CSS variables in `:root` at the top of the module file
- Main component class comes after variable definitions
- Use nested selectors for component elements (modern CSS nesting is supported)
- Group related styles together in this order:
  1. `:root` variable definitions
  2. Base component class (`.sc-component`)
  3. Component element classes (`.sc-component-element`)
  4. Variant selectors (`.sc-component[data-variant='...']`)
  5. Appearance selectors (`.sc-component[data-appearance='...']`)
  6. State selectors (`:hover`, `:disabled`, `:focus`, etc.)
  7. Modifier selectors (`.sc-component[data-rounded='true']`, etc.)
- Example structure:
  ```css
  :root {
      /* Variables */
  }
  .sc-component {
      /* Base styles */
  }
  .sc-component[data-variant='primary'] {
      /* Variant overrides */
  }
  .sc-component:hover {
      /* State styles */
  }
  ```

## File Organization

- Component files: `ComponentName.jsx` and `ComponentName.module.css` in the same directory
- Import CSS module in the JSX file: `import './ComponentName.module.css';`
- Use `cn()` utility for className composition: `className={cn('sc-component', className)}`
- Import `cn` from `@/utilities`: `import { cn } from '@/utilities';`
- Example JSX:
  ```jsx
  import { cn } from '@/utilities';
  import './Component.module.css';
  
  export const Component = ({ className, variant, rounded, ...props }) => {
      return (
          <div 
              className={cn('sc-component', className)}
              data-variant={variant}
              data-rounded={rounded}
              {...props}
          >
              {children}
          </div>
      );
  };
  ```

## Accessibility & Best Practices

- ALWAYS include focus states for keyboard navigation
- Use semantic HTML elements (button, input, details, etc.)
- Support `prefers-reduced-motion` (handled by default theme - `--animation-speed` becomes `0ms`)
- Ensure sufficient color contrast (use scale 10-12 for backgrounds and scale 1-3 for text - theme colors automatically switch between light and dark modes when configured correctly)
- Include `:focus-visible` for visible focus indicators
- Example focus styles:
  ```css
  .sc-component:focus,
  .sc-component:focus-visible {
      outline: 2px solid var(--base-1);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px var(--primary-11);
  }
  ```

## Example Pattern Reference

### CSS Module (Component.module.css)
```css
:root {
    /* Component Sizing & Spacing - Using design system tokens as defaults */
    --component-padding: var(--spacing-padding-2);
    --component-gap: var(--spacing-gap-2);
    
    /* Component Typography */
    --component-font-size: var(--font-size-2);
    --component-font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    --component-line-height: var(--font-line-height);
    
    /* Component Theming - Default colors */
    --component-theme-color: var(--base-10);
    --component-bg-color: var(--base-1);
    --component-text-color: var(--base-12);
    --component-border-color: var(--base-12);
}

/* Component CSS Module */
.sc-component {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    background-color: var(--component-bg-color);
    color: var(--component-text-color);
    padding: var(--component-padding);
    gap: var(--component-gap);
    font-size: var(--component-font-size);
    font-weight: var(--component-font-weight);
    line-height: var(--component-line-height);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius-0);
    transition: all var(--animation-speed) ease-in-out;
}

.sc-component-content {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--spacing-gap-1);
}

/* Data attribute selectors for state */
.sc-component[data-variant='primary'] {
    --component-theme-color: var(--primary-10);
    --component-border-color: var(--primary-10);
}

.sc-component[data-variant='alert'] {
    --component-theme-color: var(--alert-10);
    --component-border-color: var(--alert-10);
}

.sc-component[data-appearance='outline'] {
    background: transparent;
    border: 3px solid var(--component-theme-color);
    color: var(--component-theme-color);
}

.sc-component[data-rounded='true'] {
    border-radius: var(--border-radius-rounded);
}

.sc-component[data-size='sm'] {
    padding: var(--spacing-padding-1) var(--spacing-padding-2);
    font-size: var(--font-size-1);
}

.sc-component:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--component-theme-color) 90%, white);
}

.sc-component:disabled {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--component-theme-color) 50%, transparent);
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.6;
}

.sc-component:focus,
.sc-component:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--base-1);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px var(--primary-11);
}
```

### JSX Component (Component.jsx)
```jsx
import { forwardRef } from 'react';
import { cn } from '@/utilities';
import './Component.module.css';

export const Component = forwardRef(function Component(
    { 
        children, 
        className, 
        variant = 'base',
        appearance = 'solid',
        rounded = false,
        size = 'md',
        disabled = false,
        ...props 
    },
    ref,
) {
    return (
        <div
            ref={ref}
            className={cn('sc-component', className)}
            data-variant={variant}
            data-appearance={appearance}
            data-rounded={rounded ? 'true' : 'false'}
            data-size={size}
            disabled={disabled}
            {...props}
        >
            <div className="sc-component-content">
                {children}
            </div>
        </div>
    );
});
```

## Files to Reference

When creating or modifying components, reference these files for patterns:
- `lib/components/Theme/themes/default-theme.css` - Design token definitions and semantic color mappings
- `lib/components/Button/Button.module.css` - Comprehensive example with variants, appearances, sizes, and states
- `lib/components/Accordion/Accordion.module.css` - Variant pattern example
- `lib/components/Badge/Badge.module.css` - Appearance variant and data attribute examples
- `lib/components/Input/Input.module.css` - Form component styling patterns

## Summary Checklist

When creating or modifying a component, ensure:
- [ ] CSS Module file exists: `ComponentName.module.css`
- [ ] All classes use `sc-` prefix
- [ ] CSS variables defined in `:root` grouped by category
- [ ] Design tokens used (no hardcoded values)
- [ ] Colors from spiffy-colors semantic mappings
- [ ] Data attributes used for variants, appearance, size, rounded, etc.
- [ ] Hover, disabled, focus states included
- [ ] `color-mix()` used for state variations
- [ ] Transitions use `--animation-speed`
- [ ] Focus states for accessibility
- [ ] JSX uses `cn()` utility and sets data attributes
